  "task_version": 2,
  "query": "Every gaming keyboard I look at advertises 8000Hz polling, optical switches with supposedly zero debounce delay, and full N-key rollover like they're life-changing. My friend insists that past a basic level none of it is humanly perceptible, yet buyer reviews are full of people swearing their aim got better the day the box arrived. Before I pay a premium for the spec-sheet flagship, I want to know which of these features are physically real advantages, which are placebo, and whether there's a sensibly priced board that already has the ones that genuinely matter.",
